Experimental code with module loading. Initially needed for viewing comments on online streams (e.g., YouTube or Twitch) and supporting streamers.

The startup script creates a venv and loads it.

At this stage, there are a lot of bugs, but dependencies should load automatically at startup.
To check the chat, you need to specify the channel in the file /models/twitchChatreader.py.

pyenv prepare (ubuntu)
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y \
  build-essential \
  libssl-dev \
  zlib1g-dev \
  libbz2-dev \
  libreadline-dev \
  libsqlite3-dev \
  curl \
  libncursesw5-dev \
  xz-utils \
  tk-dev \
  libxml2-dev \
  libxmlsec1-dev \
  libffi-dev \
  liblzma-dev \
  git
curl https://pyenv.run | bash

